# Vollyio environment variables.
# Copy to .env.local and fill in real values. Never commit .env.local or any real secret.

# --- Supabase (public: safe to expose to the browser) ---
# Project URL and anon/publishable key from the Supabase dashboard.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# --- Coaching service (server-side only; never exposed to the browser) ---
# ONE key now, for everything (D-098). There is no second provider: the clip
# read, player spotting, coach chat and the weekly plan all go through the
# gateway, so this single prepaid balance is the whole app's model budget and
# the app cannot see it. Traffic on any one surface can starve the others; the
# per-account quotas bound one player, never the aggregate.
# Absent, every surface fails the way a provider outage does: analyze answers
# the calm 502/503 and counts nothing against the player, spotting returns an
# empty candidate list so the tap-anywhere path still works, and coach chat and
# the weekly plan return 503 before spending a quota unit.
# DEPLOY ORDER: this must exist in the target environment BEFORE the code that
# reads it. Serverless env is snapshotted at deploy time, so shipping the code
# first means every coach message and every analysis fails until a redeploy.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your-coaching-service-key

# --- Site URL (used for metadataBase, canonical URLs, sitemap, robots) ---
# Local dev defaults to http://localhost:3000 when unset.
# On Vercel, VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL is provided automatically and used as a fallback.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Support mailbox (public: shown on the legal pages and footer Contact link) ---
# Set to a real, monitored mailbox in production; the Privacy Policy promises
# deletion within 30 days of an email to this address. Falls back to
# support@<SITE_URL host> when unset (see lib/site.ts).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_EMAIL=

# --- Transactional email (server-side only; never exposed to the browser) ---
# Resend API key scoped to sending on the verified send.vollyio.com domain.
# Leave unset locally: sendEmail() reports a failed send and nothing is delivered.
# Auth email and the welcome email do NOT read this one. They are sent from the
# supabase/functions/send-email and send-welcome edge functions, which carry
# their own RESEND_API_KEY secret set on the Supabase project.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Sender identity for product mail. Must be an address on a domain verified with
# the email provider or every send is rejected. Defaults to the value below.
RESEND_FROM=Vollyio <noreply@send.vollyio.com>

# --- Billing (docs/billing.md is the model; docs/deploy.md the rollout order) ---
# Everything here is server-only except NEXT_PUBLIC_UPGRADE_URL, which is
# client-visible by definition and is the only billing value that may be.

# Bypasses row security on every table. Read by lib/supabase/service.ts alone;
# its two sanctioned importers are recorded in docs/security.md rule 10.
# Leave unset locally: the webhook fails closed and telemetry stays null.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Payment provider API key. Read only by lib/stripe.ts.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# Webhook endpoint signing secret. Absent, the webhook returns 500 and applies
# nothing; there is deliberately no unverified branch. Set this BEFORE the key
# above in any fresh environment (docs/deploy.md explains the ordering).
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# One recurring price per offer. Not secrets, but deliberately not NEXT_PUBLIC_:
# a client-visible price id is the shape of the bug where the caller decides
# what to charge. The client posts an offer KEY; the server maps it to one of
# these.
#
# STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY is the one checkout REQUIRES: unset, `stripeConfigured()`
# is false and no button renders. WEEKLY just drops a choice from the picker,
# and DOWNSELL just suppresses the exit-intent modal.
#
# The retired single STRIPE_PRICE_ID is gone on purpose and is NOT read as a
# fallback: it points at a price found archived on 2026-08-12, and an archived
# price cannot back a checkout session.
STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_WEEKLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_DOWNSELL=

# Set to "true" only after the provider dashboard holds a Terms of Service URL
# (dashboard-only setting); with the URL absent, session creation FAILS.
# See lib/stripe.ts for the recovery story.
STRIPE_TOS_CONSENT=

# --- Optional feature flags ---
# Set to "true" to return canned coaching responses without calling the coaching service
# (useful for local development and tests). Leave unset in production.
AI_MOCK=

# "true" makes Pro buyable (checkout and portal stop answering 503). One of the
# two switches; the other is ENFORCE_FREE_CAP below. See docs/billing.md D-066.
BILLING_ENABLED=

# "true" makes the monthly allowance actually refuse a rep. Deliberately inert
# unless BILLING_ENABLED and NEXT_PUBLIC_UPGRADE_URL are also set, so a cap can
# never engage in a configuration where a player could not buy past it.
ENFORCE_FREE_CAP=

# Where the "allowance used" response sends a player (the Settings plan card).
# Setting it is the second key that arms enforcement.
NEXT_PUBLIC_UPGRADE_URL=

# Coach chat is ON by default as of 2026-08-06. Set this to exactly "false" to
# take it away: that closes the nav entry, the page and /api/coach together.
# The switch exists because one prepaid balance pays for every model call in
# the app and coach is the highest-frequency path on it, so chat traffic is the
# thing most likely to starve analysis. NEXT_PUBLIC is inlined at build time,
# so changing this needs a redeploy to take effect.
NEXT_PUBLIC_COACH_ENABLED=

# Recipient of the spend-backstop alert mail. Unset silences the mail; it does
# not disable the backstop.
OWNER_ALERT_EMAIL=


# Model routing is NOT an environment variable. The two ids are
# checked-in constants in lib/ai/client.ts (see decisions.md D-004 and D-098),
# deliberately: a typo in a model string would surface as a runtime 404 on a
# paid call path rather than at build time.

# Deliberately ABSENT, and each was here until 2026-08-11 describing something
# that does not exist:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID / META_CAPI_TOKEN - no pixel or Conversions API
#     call exists anywhere in app/, lib/ or components/. An operator reading
#     this file would have believed conversion tracking was wired. It is not.
#     Adding it later also changes the Data safety form Play cross-checks.
#   ANALYZE_MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD - its guard lib/ai/budget.ts was deleted in
#     D-104 on 2026-08-06. The prepaid balance is read directly instead now,
#     see lib/ai/credits.ts.
